 4. 📈 Charted: America&#x27;s income record 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Census Bureau. Chart: Russell Contreras/Axios U.S. household income hit a record in 2025, Axios' Russell Contreras writes from new census data . 

 Inflation-adjusted household income rose 2.6% to $87,460 in 2025, the highest since records began in 1967. The official poverty rate fell for a third straight year, dropping slightly to 10.2%. 👓 Between the lines: The economy delivered historic topline numbers, but the gains weren't spread evenly.

 Income among the wealthiest 10% of Americans rose 1.7%, while income among the bottom 10% showed no significant change. Share this story . 

 
 
