 5. 🚀 Pentagon confirms weapons in space 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Axios Future of Defense author Colin Demarest writes: 

 The U.S. has space weapons in orbit right now, Air Force Secretary Troy Meink said this week at the Air, Space &amp; Cyber Conference in National Harbor, Md.

 Why it matters: The declaration is a first and marks a significant shift in how the world discusses such systems, which are considered highly sensitive and provocative. "We are increasing readiness against existing threats, and the United States has on-orbit space control weapons capable of defending the Joint Force against hostile adversary action," Meink said Monday.

 Pressed by reporters, he wouldn't elaborate. Share this story . 

 
 
