 7. 💸 Stat du jour 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A fighter jet takes off during nighttime operations from the flight deck of the USS George Washington in the Arabian Sea on Saturday. Photo: Ed Ou/Reuters The war against Iran has cost the Pentagon more than $38 billion through Aug. 1, according to a new assessment from the Congressional Budget Office .

 That amount reflects the costs of replacing munitions and equipment lost in battle, increased flying hours, other operations and increased fuel costs. The war will continue to cost $3 billion a month or more, depending on the intensity of fighting.

 🏛️ The House late yesterday voted for the third time — and again failed — to end the war, and renegade Rep. Thomas Massie (R-Ky.) introduced a resolution to impeach Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth.

