 8. 🚩 1 fun thing: Fastest-growing sport 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: NFHS . Map: Brad Jennings/Axios Girls' flag football has become the fastest-growing high school sport, as tens of thousands take up a game that barely had a varsity footprint a few years ago, Axios' Brad Jennings writes. 

 More than 102,000 girls played high school flag football in 2025-26, a 551% increase in the past four years, according to the National Federation of State High School Associations . In 2024, just 12 states sanctioned high school girls flag football, viewed as a safer, more accessible version of America's most popular spectator sport.

 Today, 23 states plus D.C. sanction it as an official varsity sport , and 3,990 schools reported participants in 2025-26. Share this story . 

 
 
